KZ3 patch 2187 (rsx stutter Task 0, diagnostics only, guest-invisible, every output behind a switch, default OFF):
whole-run attribution of long frames. Off = no new output and no new work beyond a few cached-int tests; the four
changes below touch no guest state.
1. RSX_PRESENT_QPC_STREAM=1: ported from Killzone 2 patch 6073 (same author, MIT; port/patches/6073-present-qpc-stream-whole-run.patch
   of the Killzone 2 port). New libs/video/rsx_present_stream.h (pure C, host-tested): the CSV scratch\present_qpc_<pid>.csv
   is opened at renderer init and each batch of 64 presents is appended and flushed on the present thread, so a killed
   run keeps all but its last 63 presents (the guest-frame-2293 endpoint of the one-shot dump is dropped while the stream
   is on). Extra comment line '# clock qpc=<ticks> filetime=<100 ns since 1601 UTC>' ties the QPC to the wall clock.
   Columns are those of the shutdown dump (the dump itself is untouched).
2. RSX_ATTRIB=1 (one switch for all attribution lines, QPC ticks everywhere = the CSV's clock):
   [pso-await] qpc= key= packed=0|1|2 ms= class=warm-unbuilt|unknown   (rsx_live_draw.c, ld_apso_await(idx, packed))
   [pso-cover] <frame|exit> ...  (every 256 frames and at ld_pl_shutdown; counters in g_ld_cov + g_pt/g_ld_pl)
   [vblank] ...  every 10 s (cellGcmSys.c + new libs/video/rsx_stutter_diag.h, pure C, host-tested; printed by port/kz3/main.cpp)
   [pump] gap lines get qpc= and the frame thread's time per call (drain/present/pump/idle) (port/kz3/main.cpp, same patch set)
Host test: tools/smoke/test_stutter_diag.sh.
